{
  "format": "patchkamer-tunes",
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "device": "nl.patchkamer.graincloud",
  "name": "Grain Cloud Styles",
  "author": "Freek van Gool",
  "license": "CC0-1.0",
  "description": "Granular textures for Grain Cloud, in ten styles. Almost every tune uses the built-in Wave source (choir, organ, saw, glass, noise, sine), so it sounds on its own: Cloud tunes make an endless texture, the others are played with notes (C4 plays at the original pitch; with the Wave source A3 does). A few tunes use the Live source and work as effects: they process the sound on the In (source) input and are silent without a cable (Stutter Cloud, Micro Slicer, Pitch Scatter, Reverse Chop, Warped Cassette, Freeze Echo, Smear Cloud). Every tune sets the whole state.",
